cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Skin Cancer CNN Benchmark: a reproducible comparison of seven convolutional architectures for dermoscopic lesion classification"
abstract: >-
  A single-protocol benchmark of seven convolutional architectures (AlexNet, VGG-16,
  VGG-19, GoogLeNet/Inception-v3, ResNet-50, DenseNet-121 and EfficientNet-B0) on
  binary malignant/benign dermoscopic lesion classification. Every architecture is
  trained under identical folds, seeds, augmentation and class weighting, scored with
  threshold-free and operating-point metrics, and reported with bootstrap confidence
  intervals, so that differences in the table are attributable to the backbone rather
  than to the harness.
